  "doc.title": "How a CPU Guesses Ahead · an essay you can play with",
  "doc.desc": "A branch takes a dozen cycles to resolve, and a CPU does not wait: it guesses, gains when right and starts over when wrong. How does it guess so well? Why can one CPU have hundreds of instructions in flight? And why does the guessing leak secrets? Ten models: 1-bit and 2-bit counters, the sorted array, gshare, TAGE, the return stack, superscalar issue, renaming and the reorder buffer, window size, and a toy machine for Spectre.",
  "nav.back": "← Knowledge Index",
